course: dictionary
lesson: 344
title: Words that come round again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Annual means happening once every year. «An annual check-up is a routine visit to catch problems early, even when you feel fine.» You go once a year, even when you feel well, so annual tells you how often it happens.
explain: Annual can also mean for a whole year, as in annual rainfall or an annual salary. Read the words around it and look for a time word, like year or month. Then ask: how often does this happen, or how long does it last?
explain: «Annual leave is paid holiday from work; most full-time workers get a few weeks of it a year, bank holidays included.» Here annual tells you that the holiday is a yearly amount. Try your meaning in the sentence: a yearly holiday from work still makes sense, so you have found it.
fact: Annual means happening once every year, or lasting for a whole year.
fact: «An annual check-up» is a routine visit to catch problems early, even when you feel fine.
fact: «Annual leave» is paid holiday from work, and most full-time workers get a few weeks of it a year.
fact: An annual plant grows, flowers and dies in one year.
fact: In the UK, an annual is a thick children's book with comics and puzzles that comes out once a year.
exercise: «Our annual sports day is in June.» What does annual mean? | Happens only once, never again | Lasts for one hour | *Happens once every year | Happens every day
exercise: «The annual rainfall here is high.» What does annual tell you about the rainfall? | It is very loud | It falls only in summer | *It is counted over a whole year | It falls only in one hour
exercise: Find and copy the word that means happening once a year: «The annual check-up is at the clinic.» | visit | clinic | check-up | *annual
test: What does «annual leave» mean? | A short walk around the park | *Paid holiday from work, given each year | Time spent at school each week | Leaving a room quickly
test: In the UK, what is a thick children's book with comics and puzzles, out once a year, called? | A map | *An annual | A menu | A dictionary
exam: Maya's dentist says, «Come back for your annual check-up.» How often should Maya go? | *Once a year | Every day | Only if she has toothache | Once every ten years
